From 0cb3f5449e3cd9ed91e20cb926c5b67d796bcf52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:09:19 +0000
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: add AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 board

Add the board DTS/dtsi for the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 (AVM codename
"seale", HW221), a GRX350-based DSL gateway, and the matching
built-in-DTB Kconfig option (the AVM EVA bootloader does not pass a
DTB, so the kernel carries one).

Board description highlights:

 - 128 MiB DDR at physical 0x20000000 (EVA layout).

 - Macronix MX30LF1GE8AB NAND on EBU chip-select 1 (data window at
   0x17c00000), using the chip's on-die BCH ECC via the legacy
   "nand-ecc-mode" string property (the modern "nand-ecc-engine"
   binding takes a phandle, which cannot name the on-die engine),
   with the AVM partition layout.

 - Reserved-memory carve-outs for the CBM packet-buffer pools
   (18 MiB standard + 8 MiB jumbo, no-map) and the cbm node enabled
   with those pools attached.

 - GPHY firmware loader node (lantiq,phy-xrx500) loading the LAN
   PHY11G firmware into GPHYs 2-5 through the RCU reset provider,
   and the GSWIP MDIO bus with PHY addresses aligned to the
   datapath port numbering. Front-panel LAN port N connects to
   GPHY (6-N) on this board.

 - avm-hw-revision node matching the vendor firmware's expectations.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
